### AI Assistant Behavior for Design Docs

**During DESIGN-FLOW mode:**
- ✅ Read `docs/design/` files before making design decisions
- ✅ Reference existing tokens and patterns
- ✅ Update design files when new decisions are made

**During BUILD-SCREEN mode:**
- ✅ Read `docs/design/` files before implementing UI
- ✅ Use documented tokens, patterns, and conventions
- ✅ Update `design-patterns.md` when new component patterns emerge

**During DESIGN-REVIEW mode:**
- ✅ Read `docs/design/` files as evaluation baseline
- ✅ Check implementation against documented system
- ✅ Update `design-decisions.md` with review findings

**During CLEAN-SWEEP mode:**
- ✅ Verify UI code matches documented design system
- ✅ Flag deviations from documented patterns
- ✅ Update design docs if patterns were intentionally changed

**Cross-session consistency:**
- ✅ ALWAYS read `docs/design/` at session start for UI work
- ✅ NEVER make design decisions that contradict documented patterns without updating docs
- ✅ Treat design docs as the source of truth for visual decisions

### Project-Level Design Rule

When `docs/design/` files are created, **also scaffold a project-level rule** at `.cursor/rules/design-system.mdc` that points the agent to those files every session.

**Why:** Design docs are only useful if the agent reads them. A short `alwaysApply: true` rule ensures the agent loads the design context at the start of every session automatically, without the user having to mention it.

**Create `.cursor/rules/design-system.mdc` when:**
- The first `docs/design/*.md` file is created
- A design system, CSS framework config (e.g., `tailwind.config.ts`), or token set is established

**Update `.cursor/rules/design-system.mdc` when:**
- New design doc files are added to `docs/design/`
- The CSS framework config file path changes
- Design doc files are renamed or removed

**Template:**

```markdown
---
alwaysApply: true
---
These files outline the design of this project:

docs/design/design-system.md
docs/design/design-patterns.md
docs/design/design-decisions.md
docs/design/layout-conventions.md
docs/design/interaction-patterns.md

- Read them at session start for any UI work.
- Use them when making design changes to ensure consistency.
- Update them as design decisions are made (tokens, patterns, layout, interactions).
- Ensure the CSS framework config (e.g., tailwind.config.ts) matches the design system.
```

**Rules for scaffolding:**
- Only list files that actually exist (don't list files that haven't been created yet)
- Add the CSS framework config line only if one exists in the project
- Keep it short: the rule is a pointer, not a duplicate of the docs
- The rule should reference `docs/design/` files, never inline design tokens directly

## Quality Checklist

- [ ] Header includes date, status, owner
- [ ] Markdown is properly formatted
- [ ] Document is in correct directory
- [ ] Follows naming conventions
- [ ] File moved with terminal command (if applicable)
- [ ] Design docs updated if UI decisions changed
